WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.389
Kernel ridge regression helps explain generalization,

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:08.365
and tuning a network's last layer behaves like it
with a finite-rank kernel.

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:13.340
But classical bounds are far too loose here: they
keep the ridge above zero,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.660
give only upper bounds, and go vacuous as
regularization vanishes.
